# Full original-frontend observation comparison v15

The isolated v7 profile completes full native cold/incremental equality while
actually reusing original frontend observations for **153 of 154 Python files**.
Only the authored comment change in `pyparsing/helpers.py` is reanalyzed. It
reuses **3,885 original symbols and 52,977 original edges**, extracting 772 edges
from the changed file. Pytest analysis/unification and whole-inventory graph
resolution rerun.

The independent audit compares exact serialized state and root, all **67,872
actual blocks / 112,728,034 bytes per output**, and the complete original
observation sidecar. Changed cold and incremental outputs agree exactly. The
state, root and every block also equal the retained v13 cold output. Native
scope remains **286 regular files, 154 Python files, one opaque symlink,
11,701,447 changed-source bytes, 3,957 symbols and 55,859 graph edges**. Ten native
source-read controls pass across the three workers. No source omissions,
provider calls, token savings or execution reuse are claimed.

Each original-observation sidecar contains **53,753,923 bytes**, separate from
the native bundle. The exact bound parent sidecar is read and decoded by the
incremental worker; the returned changed sidecar is byte-identical to cold. Only
the changed file's original observations differ from the parent. Its additional
storage and preparation work are material costs.

| Work | Process wall seconds |
|---|---:|
| Original v13 baseline preparation, retained paid receipt | 656.008467 |
| New full baseline observation bootstrap | 231.354099 |
| Changed cold, v7 | 440.275719 |
| Changed incremental, v7 | 607.970902 |

All three new workers finish within their prospective **900-second** bounds.
Bootstrap and changed cold start concurrently on the shared host; incremental
starts after successful bootstrap and exact parent binding. New worker schedule
wall time is 839.327665 seconds, with 0.533272 seconds of separately measured
enrollment/copy/guard/freeze setup. Overlapping process times must not be summed
as elapsed time, and nested stages must not be added again to process totals.

The new baseline bootstrap scans all original source and emits its sidecar,
then restores the exact original baseline state and all blocks, proves its new
state serialization identical, and fully verifies the bundle before reuse.
That native restoration/full verification takes 115.553456 seconds; the worker
also retains its subsequent 46.176903-second full verification and persistence.
The original 656.008467-second preparation is not treated as free.

Incremental includes **105.261605 seconds** of actual state/bundle restoration
and full re-verification. Reading the parent sidecar takes 0.024210 seconds;
typed observation restoration, native scanning, current graph resolution and
sidecar encoding are included together in the **55.519689-second** scan stage.
The concurrent cold scan stage takes **64.576213 seconds**. Incremental bundle
build takes 390.254414 seconds, full verification 48.819131 seconds and
persistence 4.726581 seconds. Cold process time remains lower than incremental
process time in this observation. No general incremental speedup is inferred.

`frontend_observations_validation_v7/summary.json` contains ten full-output
equality cases and sixteen rejection/fallback checks, including inventory
changes, original exact confidence restoration, pytest changes and stale source
bytes. An independent read-only review is retained in
`frontend_observations_v7_independent_review.json`. Runtime profile admission is
external: the native cache helper receives its declared profile hash, while the
full worker independently hashes every enrolled runtime source before and after
execution. Expected sidecar CIDs must come from accepted honest producer
receipts; no theorem that arbitrary cached observations follow from source is
claimed.

The separately retained `unresolved_import_reuse_v6_v7/summary.json` narrows the
older guard's scope: adding a previously missing imported module leaves v6
incremental confidence conservative while cold becomes exact. V7 preserves the
original observation and equals cold. This does not alter v14's completed exact
comment-only comparison; v6 is not a general lossless incremental solution.
Neither discrepancy establishes an execution-soundness failure.

Authoritative outputs are `results_v15_full_pyparsing_frontend_observations/summary.json`,
`full_pyparsing_frontend_observations_v15_audit.json`,
`FULL_PYPARSING_ORIGINAL_FRONTENDS_PROTOCOL_V15.md`,
`runtime_frontend_observations_v7_manifest.json`, and the versioned driver,
materializer, patch and source-observation design memo. All earlier profiles and
failures remain unchanged.
